 # Decision Log
 
+## 2026-08-27 - Container Rig Proof Rejected As Animation Solution
+
+**Status:** visual owner rejection; technical hierarchy retained only as a
+diagnostic.
+
+The isolated rig proof shows Phaser parent-child containers, but it does not
+solve the visible animation problem. The raster pieces were not authored for a
+cutout rig, their static pivots describe source canvases rather than visible
+joints or foot contacts, and per-part tweens let weight and grounding drift.
+The result is therefore a moved-apart sprite assembly, not a convincing
+cartoon performance.
+
+The next animation proof must start with rig-ready artwork and a real
+authoring/runtime pipeline. More numeric transforms inside Phaser would only
+repeat the rejected approach at larger scale. Godot, DragonBones and a
+whole-body frame pipeline remain candidates; no renderer is selected here.
+
